   "page": 4
  },
  {
   "name": "Constant current, maximum",
   "expr": "IO(MAX) = VREF/R1 + IADJ = 1.25V/R1",
   "where": {
    "VREF": "reference voltage, 1.25 V",
    "R1": "fixed series resistor",
    "IADJ": "adjust pin current"
   },
   "note": "The right-hand form drops the IADJ term.",
   "page": 4
  },
  {
   "name": "Constant current, minimum",
   "expr": "IO(MIN) = VREF/(R1+R2) + IADJ = 1.25V/(R1+R2)",
   "where": {
    "VREF": "reference voltage, 1.25 V",
    "R1": "fixed series resistor",
    "R2": "variable series resistor at its full value",
    "IADJ": "adjust pin current"
   },
   "note": "The right-hand form drops the IADJ term.",
   "page": 4
  }
 ],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Regulation",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Inside, a reference sits between ADJ and the non-inverting input of an error amplifier whose inverting input is on the output. The amplifier drives a Darlington pass pair from the input to the output, with a small resistor in series at the output. A protection circuit, fed by its own current source from the input, connects to both ends of that resistor."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Protection",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The part limits its own short-circuit current, protects itself against thermal overload and keeps its pass transistor inside a safe operating area. Power dissipation is internally limited. The current limit falls as the input-output differential rises: about 2.2 A typical at 15 V, 0.4 A typical at 40 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Minimum load",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The regulator needs a minimum load current to stay in regulation: 4.5 mA max at a 40 V input-output differential, and less at smaller differentials, about 0.35 mA typical at 4 V and 3.5 mA typical at 40 V (TJ = 25 °C)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Capacitors",
   "page": 4,
   "text": "With the regulator at a distance from the power supply, a 0.1 µF capacitor goes on the input. A 1 µF output capacitor improves transient response. With VOUT = 10 V at 120 Hz, ripple rejection is 65 dB typical with no adjust-pin capacitor and 80 dB typical (66 dB min) with CADJ = 10 µF."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "SOT-223 parts carry LM317AG with a data code. The other packages carry UTC over LM317A followed by L (lead free) or G (halogen free), with a lot code and a data code beneath."
  }
 ]
}
